WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.572
Look up on a sunny day. The sky is blue.

2
00:00:03.892 --> 00:00:07.674
But why? Space is black, and sunlight is white.

3
00:00:08.224 --> 00:00:12.433
Sunlight looks white, but it's really a mix of all the colours of the rainbow.

4
00:00:12.983 --> 00:00:19.312
When sunlight enters our atmosphere, it hits tiny gas molecules, mostly nitrogen and oxygen.

5
00:00:19.862 --> 00:00:22.134
Red light mostly goes straight through.

6
00:00:22.454 --> 00:00:27.671
But blue light has shorter waves, so the molecules scatter it much more, in every direction.

7
00:00:28.221 --> 00:00:33.314
So blue light bounces around the whole sky, and it comes to our eyes from every direction.

8
00:00:33.634 --> 00:00:35.490
That's why the sky looks blue.

9
00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:39.300
At sunset, the light travels through much more air.

10
00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:44.222
Most of the blue is scattered away before it reaches us, so we see orange and red.

11
00:00:44.772 --> 00:00:48.959
And why isn't the sky violet? Violet waves are even shorter.

12
00:00:49.279 --> 00:00:53.848
But the sun sends less violet light, and our eyes are less sensitive to it.

13
00:00:54.398 --> 00:00:59.257
So next time you watch a sunset, remember: you're seeing the light that survived the journey.
